Description:

Flags other than \Recent and \Deleted are now kept in step across all copies of
an email (same EMAILID) on IMAP STORE, APPEND, COPY/MOVE, LMTP/Sieve delivery
and JMAP.  A new message merges with existing copies: flags are the union, but
\Seen is set only if every copy is seen.  A COPY or MOVE within an account
keeps the flags it has.  One from another account merges every flag but \Seen,
which each copy keeps.  Copies marked \Deleted neither take nor pass on
changes.  Copies in folders the acting user can't read, or where they lack the
write (or \Seen) right, are skipped.  Replicas never propagate; the master's
changes replicate as usual.  The rules for JMAP Email/set keywords are
unchanged.


Documentation:

docsrc/rfc-support.rst, ctl_conversationsdb(8)


Config changes:

None.


Upgrade instructions:

Existing copies are not changed automatically.  Run
"ctl_conversationsdb -E <user>" (or -E -r for every user) to make them agree
(union of flags; \Seen if any copy is seen).

Run it as soon as possible after upgrading: until it has run, an APPEND or
delivery of an email whose copies disagree can mark read copies unread, as the
new copy merges with copies that aren't all seen.


